<article class="env-lemma" id="046Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/046Q">Lemma <span data-tag="046Q">78.21.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $f : (U, R, s, t, c) \to (U', R', s', t', c')$ be a morphism of groupoids in algebraic spaces over $B$. Then $f$ induces a canonical $1$-morphism of quotient stacks </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [f] : [U/R] \longrightarrow [U'/R'].  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Denote $[U/_{\! p}R]$ and $[U'/_{\! p}R']$ the categories fibred in groupoids over the base site $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ associated to the functors (<a href="/tag/044P" data-tag="044P">78.20.0.1</a>). It is clear that $f$ defines a $1$-morphism $[U/_{\! p}R] \to [U'/_{\! p}R']$ which we can compose with the stackyfication functor for $[U'/R']$ to get $[U/_{\! p}R] \to [U'/R']$. Then, by the universal property of the stackyfication functor $[U/_{\! p}R] \to [U/R]$, see Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/0436" data-tag="0436">8.9.2</a> we get $[U/R] \to [U'/R']$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>